<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!DOCTYPE ldml SYSTEM "../../common/dtd/ldml.dtd">
<!--
Proposed CLDR collation tailoring for English written in the Deseret Alphabet (en_Dsrt).
Source: Illinois Deseret Consortium, https://github.com/sigilante/idc-deseret-collation
CLDR data files are interpreted according to the LDML specification (http://unicode.org/reports/tr35/)

The tailoring states only the deltas from the CLDR root collation (DUCET order):

  1. The four diphthong letters AY, OI, OW, EW (𐐌 𐐦 𐐍 𐐧) follow the six long
     vowels and precede the six short vowels.  In root they follow the short
     vowels (AY, OW) or come last of all (OI, EW).
  2. YEE, WU, H (𐐏 𐐎 𐐐), in that order, follow ENG (𐐥) at the end of the
     alphabet.  In root they precede PEE (𐐑), in the order WU, YEE, H.

Everything else (long vowels, short vowels, the consonant series PEE..ENG, and
lowercase-before-uppercase at the tertiary level) is inherited from root.
-->
<ldml>
	<identity>
		<version number="$Revision$"/>
		<language type="en"/>
		<script type="Dsrt"/>
	</identity>
	<collations>
		<collation type="standard">
			<cr><![CDATA[
				&𐐭<𐐴<<<𐐌<𐑎<<<𐐦<𐐵<<<𐐍<𐑏<<<𐐧
				&𐑍<𐐷<<<𐐏<𐐶<<<𐐎<𐐸<<<𐐐
			]]></cr>
		</collation>
	</collations>
</ldml>
